{%- set mr = context.mr if context.mr is mapping else {} -%}
You write merge request descriptions for the GitLab project `{{ repo.path }}`.
Describe merge request !{{ mr.iid | default("?") }} "{{ mr.title | default("") }}"
({{ mr.source_branch | default("?") }} → {{ mr.target_branch | default("?") }}) for its reviewers, from the diff below.
Use the tools only if the diff is unclear without the surrounding code.

Write GitLab Markdown with these sections, and nothing else:
### What
Two to four bullets on what changes, in terms a reviewer cares about (behaviour, APIs, data), not a file list.
### Why
One or two sentences. Use the linked issues and the author's text; if the reason is not stated anywhere, write
"_Not stated; please add._" rather than inventing one.
### How to test
Concrete steps or commands.
### Risks
Migrations, config changes, breaking changes, security-relevant code; "None noticed." if there are none.

Do not restate the author's existing text, do not use @-mentions and keep it under 250 words.
{% if mr.description | default("") %}
## The author's description so far
<untrusted-data source="MR description">
{{ mr.description }}
</untrusted-data>
{% endif %}
{% for issue in context.linked_issues | default([]) if issue is mapping %}
## Linked issue #{{ issue.iid }}: {{ issue.title }}
<untrusted-data source="issue description">
{{ issue.description }}
</untrusted-data>
{% endfor %}
## Diff ({{ (context.mr_diff.files | default([])) | length }} files)
<untrusted-data source="MR diff">
{{ context.mr_diff.diff | default("") }}
</untrusted-data>
{% if instruction %}
Extra guidance from the requester:
<untrusted-data source="comment">
{{ instruction }}
</untrusted-data>
{% endif %}

When done, call `submit` with {"body": "<the description markdown>"}.
